"The sine bulb where arbitrary power values can be used, the calculation is slower than of integer powers.\n\nr  = sqrt(x*x + y*y + z*z)\nth = ArcTan2(y, x) * Float_power\nph = ArcSin(z/r) * Float_power\nr  = Power(r, Float_power)\nx  = r * cos(ph) * cos(th) + Cx\ny  = r * cos(ph) * sin(th) + Cy\nz  = Z_multiplier * r * sin(ph) + Cz" = "Sinusowi bulb, w chtërnym mòże bëc ùżëwóné lëbòwné wôrtnotë pòtãdżi; rechòwanié je pòwòlniészé jak przë całkòwitëch pòtãdżach.\n\nr  = sqrt(x*x + y*y + z*z)\nth = ArcTan2(y, x) * Float_power\nph = ArcSin(z/r) * Float_power\nr  = Power(r, Float_power)\nx  = r * cos(ph) * cos(th) + Cx\ny  = r * cos(ph) * sin(th) + Cy\nz  = Z_multiplier * r * sin(ph) + Cz";
"The triplex math sine bulb, as suggested by Daniel White and Paul Nylander.  These are fast implementions of powers of 2,3,4,5,6,7 and 8.\n\nIf you want to make an animation with smooth power changings, please use the 'Real Power' formula." = "Sinusowi bulb w triplex-matematice, zaproponowóny przez Daniela White'a ë Paula Nylandera.  To są chùtczé implementacëje pòtãdżi 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7 ë 8.\n\nGdë chcesz zrobic animacëjã z gładczima zmianama pòtãdżi, ùżëjë fòrmùłë 'Real Power'.";
"They join the formula list; they are also in the app's Formulas folder in the Files app. Without the desktop's compiler they run slower." = "Trôfiają na lëstã fòrmùłów; są téż w katalogù Formulas aplikacji w aplikacji Lopczi. Bez kòmpilatora z wersji na kòmpùtr dzejają pòwòlni.";
